  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Migration Management in Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To achieve progress on migration-related global commitments IOM proposes to establish a United Nations Network on Migration in Pakistan that will enable and best ensure effective, timely and coordinated UN country-team wide support to the GOP in the development and implementation of programmes that respond to the most pertinent needs of Pakistan, and better enable a whole-of-society and whole-of government approach. 
 
Based on close coordination with GOP, IOM has identified critical need for introducing tailored capacity building courses on migration management in Pakistan, and will provide trainings as per its flagship programme on Essentials of Migration Management covering topics such as rights and gender-based approaches to border management. 
 
IOM proposes to strengthen awareness raising efforts with a focus on the benefits of regular migration and risks of irregular migration, to provide potential migrants with accurate information on migration realities so that they are in a position to make an informed decision. Awareness raising activities are also a priority area for the GOP, as specified in their National Action Plan (2021-2025), with a specific focus on partnerships and coordination amongst various actors such as civil society, international organisations and public sector.</narrative>
  </description>
